  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it or `vite build` here, so the physics tuning and visuals are untested.\n\n- **Scene:** 15 cubes in rows of 5, 4, 3, 2 and 1 rest on a floor under the `outdoor-day` look, which supplies the lighting and shadows. A fixed camera frames the pyramid and the ball's approach.\n- **Physics:** I used Aura3D's standalone physics world (`physics.worldAsync`) instead of `app.physics`. Its `world.reset()` restores every body's exact starting position and rotation. The `app.physics` handles can't set rotation, so tumbled boxes couldn't be put back with them. I copy each body's pose to its scene node every frame.\n- **Shot:** The ball starts on the floor 11 m from the pyramid. It launches at about 21 m/s toward the pyramid 1.5 s after the first frame, with continuous collision detection on so it can't tunnel through boxes. Boxes tumble and settle under the solver.\n- **Space:** Pressing it resets all 16 bodies to their start poses and launches the ball again immediately.\n- **Loop:** A fixed 1/60 s physics step runs inside the engine's frame callback. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on the first `requestAnimationFrame` after the app is ready.\n- **Overlay:** I added a small DOM text hint, \"Space: reset and relaunch\".\n\n",
